course: dictionary
lesson: 15236
title: Sharpened: made sharp, or made stronger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sharpened» is the past form of «sharpen». When you sharpen a pencil, you make its point thinner and pointier. Once it is done, the pencil is sharpened.
explain: «The knife was sharpened by Dad before we cooked the dinner.» The clue is «before we cooked»: the knife was ready to cut when Dad finished. So sharpened means it had been made sharp.
explain: Sharpened can also describe skills or senses, not just edges: «The owl's sharpened hearing caught the mouse.» Here it means made stronger or clearer. Test it: swap in «made stronger» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Sharpen» means to make a point or edge sharper.
fact: «Sharpened» is the past form of «sharpen», and it can also be an adjective, as in «a sharpened pencil».
fact: Other forms of the same word are sharpen, sharpens and sharpening.
fact: «Sharpened» can mean made stronger or clearer, as in «sharpened skills».
exercise: «Ella used a sharpened pencil to draw the map.» What does sharpened mean here? | *Made to have a sharp point | Very long and thin | Broken in two | Covered in paint
exercise: «Her sharpened skills helped her win the spelling game.» What does sharpened mean here? | Made softer | Made dull | *Made stronger and clearer | Hidden away
exercise: «The cook sharpened the knife and sliced the bread.» Find and copy the word that is the past form of sharpen. | *sharpened | cook | sliced | bread
test: Which form of sharpen shows that something happened in the past? | *sharpened | sharpens | sharp | sharpening
test: «The sharpened knife cut through the apple.» What does sharpened tell you about the knife? | It was very heavy | It was broken | *It had been made sharp | It was painted
exam: «The owl had sharpened senses, so it heard the mouse under the snow.» What does sharpened suggest here? | Made wet | Made heavy | *Made stronger and clearer | Made broken
